From 5e93030b56745c63970faa5b7d8b5dda7dfdfdfb Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ruscher <rruscher@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 18:10:21 -0300
Subject: [PATCH 16/17] wlclient: Creates the pointer observer only when the
 seat has a pointer.

Without a pointer on the seat (headless, WLR_LIBINPUT_NO_DEVICES=1, or a
touch-only machine), the dock-apps called
ext_input_observation_manager_v1.create_pointer_observer() with a NULL
wl_pointer. libwayland refused to marshal the request, the display
connection broke and the app exited at startup.

Adds a `pointer_changed` event to the client, emitted when the seat's
pointer capability appears or disappears. Icons and XDG toplevels create
the pointer observer only if there is a pointer, and (re)create or
destroy it on that event. The observer is destroyed before the pointer is
released.

Also fixes the keyboard not being released when the seat loses the
keyboard capability: The check tested the pointer instead.

Signed-off-by: ruscher <rruscher@gmail.com>
---
 src/wlclient/icon.c         | 95 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++--------
 src/wlclient/wlclient.c     | 10 +++-
 src/wlclient/wlclient.h     |  5 ++
 src/wlclient/xdg_toplevel.c | 95 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++--------
 4 files changed, 163 insertions(+), 42 deletions(-)

